id: decisions/008-public-repo-privacy
title: "Whether the public repo is a public surface"
kind: decision-frame
record_shape: header
status: draft
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-12; drafted from the JUDGMENTS.md reversal axis 'disclosure-depth'; recommendation is an attributed inference and ratifies nothing"
version: "1.0.0"
updated: 2026-09-12
template_ref: templates/decision.yawn
principal_ref: principal:dave

axis: disclosure-depth
axis_gloss: "how much of what is known is shown: verbatim and complete, or summarised, redacted and progressively revealed"
poles:
  a: minimal-redacted-disclosure
  b: full-fidelity-disclosure
split: leaning
draft_status: full
leverage: 25.2
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(24) x split_weight(0.7) x authored_conflict_bonus(1.5)"

question: >
  Is this public repository a public surface that must carry sanitized summaries
  only, or a source record that keeps full detail, including local file paths
  and real family names?

why_it_matters: >
  agents/yawn.bot.policy.yawn says public surfaces carry no private links and
  sanitized summaries only, yet the active tree holds 15 references to
  C:/Users/dave paths and one example built on the maintainer's real family, so
  the privacy boundary is stated but not held. Once answered, every bot that
  writes a ledger or contract into this repo knows whether workspace: may name a
  local path, and a child Yawn learns whether it inherits a full-fidelity rule
  or a redaction rule.

state_snapshot:
  description: >
    17 judgments sit at minimal-redacted-disclosure (11 authored) and 7 at
    full-fidelity-disclosure (4 authored). The repository asserts both directions
    on this axis.
  attributed_to: JUDGMENTS.md
  epistemic_status: observed
  source_refs:
    - JUDGMENTS.md
    - TAXONOMY.md

lacuna:
  kind: unselected_choice
  description: >
    Whether Dave, as principal, consents to his family's real names in a public
    example, and whether the C:/ paths were deliberately published as
    documentation of a private setup or are an oversight.

options:
  - name: A
    description: >
      rule: The public repository is a public surface under
      agents/yawn.bot.policy.yawn privacy.public_surfaces. No active .yawn record
      may carry a local filesystem path, a private link, or personal data about
      anyone other than the principal. Fuller evidence lives on a private surface
      and is labelled private.
    cost: "Replace 15 C:/ paths across 8 files with labelled private pointers; re-source or downgrade references/scientific-frame.yawn and references/july-01-lock.yawn; synthesize or consent-mark examples/dave-good-dad-objective-holon.yawn."
    risk: "Automation contracts lose the literal workspace path their runs depend on, so the contract and the run diverge."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "A test in tests/ (or an extension to scripts/validate-public-surfaces.py) that fails on any C:/, /Users/ or OneDrive path in an active .yawn outside a frozen grandfather list that may only shrink."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0031"
      - "J0064"
      - "J0087"
      - "J0158"
      - "J0183"
      - "J0184"
  - name: B
    description: >
      rule: The repository is the source of record and keeps full fidelity. Local
      paths, real names and conflicting sources are recorded as they are;
      compression is a View. Nothing in the repo is redacted.
    cost: "agents/yawn.bot.policy.yawn privacy.public_surfaces must be rewritten to exclude the repository itself; the redaction promise in blocked_effects ('expose private evidence') is withdrawn."
    risk: "Private paths and family names are already public; the rule would ratify an exposure rather than choose it."
    reversibility: false
    proof_needed: "None can enforce this; the record would be the policy rewrite."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0144"
      - "J0286"
      - "J0365"
      - "J0392"
      - "J0644"
      - "J0680"
  - name: C
    description: >
      rule: The repository keeps full fidelity for claims, contradictions and
      provenance (both sources kept, contradictions survive merge, source detail
      preserved). Two named classes are redacted everywhere: local filesystem paths,
      which become a labelled private pointer (private_evidence: labelled, with a
      reachable public stand-in or none), and personal data about people who are not
      the principal, which is synthesized as the sibling examples already do unless
      the principal records consent by name.
    cost: "Same file edits as A for paths; the family example gains either a consent field or pseudonyms; no change to the full-fidelity rules on the B side."
    risk: "The consent field is written by the same person whose data is not at issue, so it proves authorship, not the children's consent."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "A test in tests/ that fails on C:/, /Users/ or OneDrive paths in active .yawn files outside a shrinking grandfather list, plus a check that examples carrying a real person's name carry synthetic_non_personal_example or a principal consent field."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0031"
      - "J0087"
      - "J0144"
      - "J0286"
      - "J0365"

recommendation:
  option_ref: C
  confidence: 0.75
  epistemic_status: inferred
  authority: none
  reasoning: >
    The authored rules on the two sides are not actually in conflict: side A
    governs projections (smaller surfaces may hide but not lie; public gets
    summaries) and side B governs source records (keep both sources, keep
    contradictions, keep resolution). The only real collision is J0644, the one
    behaviour-proven, outcome-attached judgment on the axis, where the artifacts
    publish local Windows paths against the stated policy, and J0392, the
    unsynthesized family example. GROUND_TRUTH FACT 19 corroborates 15 unreachable
    C:/ paths, one of them the sole first source of a record marked source-backed.
    C keeps every authored rule intact and writes down the two classes that the
    artifacts currently violate.

target_condition:
  mode: decide
  proposed_by: agent-on-behalf
  affected_principals:
    - principal:dave
  ratification_status: proposed
  sufficient_when:
    - "A test in tests/ fails on any C:/Users path in an active .yawn outside a named grandfather list, the list may only shrink, and the suite passes."
    - "references/scientific-frame.yawn either cites a reachable source or its proof.status no longer reads source-backed."
    - "examples/dave-good-dad-objective-holon.yawn carries a principal consent field or is synthesized like examples/participation-choice.yawn (synthetic_non_personal_example: true)."
    - "Every automation workspace: or source_repo: that named a local path now names a labelled private pointer."

choice:
  selected_by: ""
  option_ref: ""
  authority_ref: ""

proof:
  covers:
    - target_condition
    - options
  falsifier: >
    A new automation contract lands with workspace: a Windows user-profile path and npm test
    stays green.
  status: proposed

resolves:
  - "J0031"
  - "J0064"
  - "J0087"
  - "J0158"
  - "J0183"
  - "J0184"
  - "J0144"
  - "J0286"
  - "J0365"
  - "J0392"
  - "J0644"
  - "J0680"

boundary:
  - "confidence cannot ratify an objective; this record proposes and Dave decides"
  - "the REVEALED judgments cited here describe what artifacts do, not what Dave chose"

source:
  template: templates/decision.yawn
  axis: TAXONOMY.md
  inventory: JUDGMENTS.md
